    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class in the project, and both its tests pass along with a green build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field as a derived property on the owner representation, following the existing convention for computed fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `membershipTier` property (read-only, enum `BRONZE`/`SILVER`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets a typed `MembershipTierEnum`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\", expression = \"java(resolveMembershipTier(owner))\")` and a small single-responsibility `resolveMembershipTier` method: returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 **and** an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`. The email check reuses the same \"present and non-blank\" notion, and the null-safe `Integer.valueOf(0).equals(...)` guards against a missing count.\n\nThe logic lives in the mapper alongside the other derived-field formatters rather than being bolted onto the model, controller, or DTO. The full test suite is green.",
